id: pm-qmb6h8
title: Distinguish Vitest coverage-threshold exits from test assertion failures in combined runner verdicts
description: "A focused canonical coverage invocation reports seven test files and all 199 tests passed, but Vitest exits nonzero for the unchanged global coverage thresholds. run-tests.mjs treats that exit as a test-execution failure, combines it with the exact-source coverage refusal, and prints Test execution and exact coverage both failed with exit3. Preserve fail-closed coverage while classifying assertion execution independently from Vitest threshold exit semantics."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 2
tags: []
created_at: "2026-11-09T10:23:30.869Z"
updated_at: "2026-11-10T07:25:13.626Z"
closed_at: "2026-11-10T07:17:52.926Z"
completed_at: "2026-11-10T07:17:52.926Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 60
acceptance_criteria: Reproduce all-pass focused tests plus coverage-only failure; retain nonzero exact coverage admission and unchanged full denominator; distinguish test-only coverage-only and combined failures without parsing fragile human log strings
parent: pm-u9d0
risk: medium
confidence: 95
resolution: "Added an invocation-owned minimal Vitest reporter, defensive receipt classification, explicit reporter retention, current public reporter types and native file-level MCP attribution; documented unchanged exit semantics and sanitized evidence through audited redaction."
expected_result: "Distinguish passing assertions plus coverage refusal from actual failed, interrupted, empty or unknown evidence while retaining complete exact coverage admission and publication-safe records."
actual_result: "All 12383 active assertions across 926 files pass, with 100/100/100/100 exact coverage and zero deficits across 843 source files. Real-process negative controls retain exit 3. Static quality, project and reporter type checks, version policy, artifact budgets, package-owned changelog and final secret scan pass. Original failed attempts remain recorded."
